    "input_tokens": 11425,
    "output_tokens": 589
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 8,
   "response_text": "The mean validation accuracy is 0.87982, which is ~2.4% above the healthy upper bound of 0.8607. This is a clear and significant anomaly.\n\nThe problem is that with `opt_c: true` and `opt_c_level: 0.28`, the derived column is providing too much predictive signal. A reasonable fix would be to either:\n1. Disable `opt_c` (set to false), or\n2. Reduce `opt_c_level` significantly\n\nSince the healthy baseline is 0.8563 \u00b1 ~0.0044, and considering the mechanism of the derived column, I should propose disabling it entirely (`opt_c: false`) or setting it to 0 level. The most conservative fix is to disable it.",
